The __repr__ method in the Predicate class (lines 346-355) performs type/attribute checking without comprehensive exception handling:

```python
def __repr__(self) -> str:
    if getattr(self.func, "__name__", "<lambda>") == "<lambda>":
        return f"{self.__class__.__name__}({self.func!r})"
    if isinstance(self.func, (types.MethodType, types.BuiltinMethodType)) and (
        namespace := getattr(self.func.__self__, "__name__", None)
    ):
        return f"{self.__class__.__name__}({namespace}.{self.func.__name__})"
    if isinstance(self.func, type(str.isascii)):  # method descriptor
        return f"{self.__class__.__name__}({self.func.__qualname__})"  # LINE 353
    return f"{self.__class__.__name__}({self.func.__name__})"
```

The vulnerability on line 353 is that isinstance(self.func, type(str.isascii)) does not guarantee that __qualname__ exists.
